# Cache policy, read by Cloudflare Pages from the root of the deployed directory.
#
# The page keeps its name across deploys, so it must never be held: max-age=0
# with must-revalidate makes the browser ask every time, and the ETag turns
# almost every ask into a 304 with no body — one round trip, not one download.
#
# Everything else here is named after its own contents or never changes, so it
# gets the opposite treatment. The stylesheet goes out as style.<hash>.css (see
# build.sh): a new stylesheet is a new URL, which is what makes a year of cache
# safe. Note that this zone's Browser Cache TTL raises short max-ages to four
# hours no matter what is written here — it cannot lower long ones, which is why
# the hashed name, and not this file, is what actually keeps the site fresh.
/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/index.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/style.*.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
